## CWE rule
CWE-190 — Integer Overflow or Wraparound
Description: An arithmetic computation on externally controlled values can overflow and produce a wrong size used for allocations or indexes.
Vulnerability indicators:
- Multiplication or addition of input-derived sizes passed to malloc/calloc/realloc without an overflow check
- Conversions between signed and unsigned types on lengths
